te king exposed on a6 while Black\u2019s queen already occupies the open a-file and Black\u2019s g-pawn is poised to advance; the most forcing continuation that exploits both of those factors is the immediate pawn push that gains space and opens lines toward the king.  \n\nAll other candidate replies (king flight, queen checks along the a-file, etc.) are either illegal because of blocking units or materially inferior to the pawn thrust.\n\n\\boxed{g5g4}", "success": true, "error": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 912, "output_tokens": 132, "total_tokens": 1044}, "provider": "xai", "model_used": "grok-4.3", "requested_model": null, "invoked_at": null}, "cost": 0.00147, "accuracy": 0.0}, {"global index": "ChessInstruct_149", "prompt": "You are given a question about chess moves. Analyze the context carefully and provide the correct move.\n\nContext:\nGiven some set of chess moves, write the best possible move\n\nQuestion:\n{{\"moves\": [\"g1f3\", \"d7d5\", \"g2g3\", \"g8f6\", \"f1g2\", \"g7g6\", \"e1g1\", \"f8g7\", \"c2c4\", \"d5c4\", \"d1a4\", \"c7c6\", \"a4c4\", \"a7a5\", \"d2d3\", \"f6d5\", \"c4c2\", \"e8g8\", \"a2a3\", \"e7e5\", \"b1d2\", \"f8e8\", \"d2c4\", \"a5a4\", \"e2e4\", \"d5b6\", \"c1g5\", \"d8c7\", \"c4b6\", \"c7b6\", \"g5e3\", \"b6a5\", \"b2b4\", \"a4b3\", \"c2b3\", \"g7f8\", \"f1c1\", \"h7h6\", \"a3a4\", \"b8a6\", \"e3b6\", \"a5b4\", \"b3b4\", \"f8b4\", \"a4a5\", \"c6c5\"]}}\n\nInstructions:\n- State the correct chess move clearly.\n- Format your final answer as \\boxed{X}, where X is the move in standard coordinate notation (e.g., a2a3).\n- Keep your explanation or reasoning within 2\u20133 sentences.", "prediction": "grok-4.3", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The given move list reaches a position after 23 moves by each side, with Black having just played ...c6-c5. This leaves the c5-pawn hanging to White\u2019s dark-squared bishop on b6. The capture Bxc5 simultaneously wins material, exploits the open c-file already occupied by the roo